{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Norm","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace.lean#L20-L75","doc":"**Unit-modulus eigenvalues from det = 1 and small real trace.**\n\nThe genuine structural content the figure-eight needs: if a complex\nnumber `λ` is a root of the real characteristic polynomial\n`x² - t·x + 1` of a `2×2` real matrix with determinant `1` and real\ntrace `t` satisfying `t² < 4`, then `‖λ‖ = 1` (unit modulus).\n\nProof: take real and imaginary parts of the root equation.  The\nimaginary part gives `λ.im·(2λ.re - t) = 0`; with `t² < 4` the root is\nnon-real (`λ.im ≠ 0`), so `λ.re = t/2`.  The real part then pins\n`λ.im² = 1 - λ.re²`, hence `normSq λ = λ.re² + λ.im² = 1`, i.e.\n`‖λ‖ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}